<https://w3id.org/DOLCE/OWL/DOLCEnaryRel#tempWhole> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#sameAs> <https://w3id.org/DOLCE/OWL/DOLCEnaryRel#tempWhole> .
<https://w3id.org/DOLCE/OWL/DOLCEnaryRel/4.5> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#sameAs> <https://w3id.org/DOLCE/OWL/DOLCEnaryRel/4.5> .
<https://w3id.org/DOLCE/OWL/DOLCEnaryRel> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Stefano Borgo, Francesco Compagno, Claudio Masolo, Emilio M. Sanfilippo, Walter Terkaj" .
<https://w3id.org/DOLCE/OWL/DOLCEnaryRel> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator> "Laure Vieu and Daniele Porello" .
<https://w3id.org/DOLCE/OWL/DOLCEnaryRel> <http://purl.org/vocab/vann/preferredNamespacePrefix> "dn" .
<https://w3id.org/DOLCE/OWL/DOLCEnaryRel> <http://purl.org/vocab/vann/preferredNamespaceUri> "https://w3id.org/DOLCE/OWL/DOLCEnaryRel#" .
<https://w3id.org/DOLCE/OWL/DOLCEnaryRel> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Ontology> .
<https://w3id.org/DOLCE/OWL/DOLCEnaryRel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "DOLCE in OWL with n-ary relations. Requires importing DOLCEbasic.\nMost of the n-ary relations are temporalised relations, e.g. mereological relations between endurants at a time (in DOLCEbasic only constant mereological relations between endurants are included), but not all, e.g., the constant sum between endurants is a ternary relation.\n\nThe treatment of n-ary relations is based on the W3C reification approach.\nhttps://www.w3.org/TR/swbp-n-aryRelations/\n\nWe introduce classes of n-ary reified relationships and an object property for each argument of the n-ary relation.\n\nE.g. for the temporalised parthood relation between two endurants at a time, the class RRelTempPart and the properties tempPart, tempWhole, rRelTime. The property rRelTime is shared by all reified temporalised relationships gathered under the class ReifiedTemporalisedRelationship" .
<https://w3id.org/DOLCE/OWL/DOLCEnaryRel> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#imports> <https://w3id.org/DOLCE/OWL/DOLCEbasic> .
<https://w3id.org/DOLCE/OWL/DOLCEnaryRel> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#sameAs> <https://w3id.org/DOLCE/OWL/DOLCEnaryRel> .
<https://w3id.org/DOLCE/OWL/DOLCEnaryRel> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#versionIRI> <https://w3id.org/DOLCE/OWL/DOLCEnaryRel/4.5> .
Annotation of the axioms is very patchy, we are still working on it, so we do not currently seek feedback on these annotations.""" <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#sameAs> "3.5 --- modified axioms of PED, NPED\nBeta version. \nWe seek feedback especially regarding whether users understand or not what are the classes and the relations and how to use them.\nFeedback regarding possible incoherences would be extremely useful as well.\nAnnotation of the axioms is very patchy, we are still working on it, so we do not currently seek feedback on these annotations." .
Beta version. 
DOLCE-basic does not include the n-ary, n>2, relations of DOLCE. For some of these relations with a time argument, a constant variant (already in DOLCE or not) is included.
E.g. for the temporalised parthood relation between two endurants at a time, the class RRelTempPart and the properties tempPart, tempWhole, rRelTime. The property rRelTime is shared by all reified temporalised relationships gathered under the class ReifiedTemporalisedRelationship""" <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#sameAs> "DOLCE in OWL with n-ary relations. Requires importing DOLCEbasic.\nMost of the n-ary relations are temporalised relations, e.g. mereological relations between endurants at a time (in DOLCEbasic only constant mereological relations between endurants are included), but not all, e.g., the constant sum between endurants is a ternary relation.\n\nThe treatment of n-ary relations is based on the W3C reification approach.\nhttps://www.w3.org/TR/swbp-n-aryRelations/\n\nWe introduce classes of n-ary reified relationships and an object property for each argument of the n-ary relation.\n\nE.g. for the temporalised parthood relation between two endurants at a time, the class RRelTempPart and the properties tempPart, tempWhole, rRelTime. The property rRelTime is shared by all reified temporalised relationships gathered under the class ReifiedTemporalisedRelationship" .
Feedback regarding possible incoherences would be extremely useful as well.
If you do add this axioms, don't forget to add the corresponding inclusion of object properties (e.g. tempPart subproperty of tempOverlapArg1 etc.)""" <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#sameAs> "To enable more inferences, you could add a subclass axiom such that RRelTempPart is a subclass of RRelTempOverlap.\n\nWe do not include it here to avoid committment on the ontological nature of relation instances. \n\nIf you do add this axioms, don't forget to add the corresponding inclusion of object properties (e.g. tempPart subproperty of tempOverlapArg1 etc.)" .
If you do add this axioms, don't forget to add the corresponding inclusion of object properties.""" <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#sameAs> "To enable more inferences, you could add a subclass axiom such that RRelTempAtomicPart is a subclass of RRelTempProperPart.\n\nWe do not include it here to avoid committment on the ontological nature of relation instances. \n\nIf you do add this axioms, don't forget to add the corresponding inclusion of object properties." .
In this constant version, the endurant x is part of the endurant y during the whole existence of y.""" <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#sameAs> "ConstantPartOf is the constant version of Temporary Parthood which is a ternary relation between two endurants x, y and a time interval t. The intended interpretation is that the endurant x is a part of the endurant y over the time interval t.\nIn this constant version, the endurant x is part of the endurant y during the whole existence of y." .
In this constant version, the endurant x participates in the perdurant y during the whole existence of y.""" <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#sameAs> "constantParticipantOf is the constant version of Participation which is a ternary relation between an endurant x, a perdurant y, and a time interval t. The intended interpretation is that x participates in y at time t. Every perdurant has at least an endurant that participates in it, and every endurant participates in some perdurant. \nIn this constant version, the endurant x participates in the perdurant y during the whole existence of y." .
In this constant version, the entity x constitutes y during the whole existence of y.""" <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#sameAs> "constantConstituentOf is the constant version of Constitution which is a ternary relation between two endurants x, y and time interval t or between two perdurants x, y and time interval t. The intended interpretation is that x constitutes y over the time interval t.\nIn this constant version, the entity x constitutes y during the whole existence of y." .
In this constant version, the region x is the quale of the quality y during the whole existence of y.""" <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#sameAs> "constantQualeOf is the constant version of Temporary Quale Of which is a ternary relation among a physical region x, a physical quality y and a time interval t or among an abstract region x, an abstract quality y and a time interval t. It relates the quality to its quale (position) at a certain time.\nIn this constant version, the region x is the quale of the quality y during the whole existence of y." .
Most of the n-ary relations are temporalised relations, e.g. mereological relations between endurants at a time (in DOLCEbasic only constant mereological relations between endurants are included), but not all, e.g., the constant sum between endurants is a ternary relation.
NB: DOLCE-basic is a module of another version of DOLCE in OWL which includes n-ary, n>2, relations of DOLCE using the W3C-recommended approach of reifying relation instances.""" <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#sameAs> "DOLCE-basic in OWL. OWL version engineered by Laure Vieu and Daniele Porello, based on DOLCE from Wonderweb Deliverable D18 and on more recent work by Claudio Masolo and the LOA. Reference to numbered axioms from D18.\nDOLCE-basic does not include the n-ary, n>2, relations of DOLCE. For some of these relations with a time argument, a constant variant (already in DOLCE or not) is included.\nNB: DOLCE-basic is a module of another version of DOLCE in OWL which includes n-ary, n>2, relations of DOLCE using the W3C-recommended approach of reifying relation instances." .
The treatment of n-ary relations is based on the W3C reification approach.
We do not include it here to avoid committment on the ontological nature of relation instances. 
We do not include it here to avoid committment on the ontological nature of relation instances. 
We do not include it here to avoid committment on the ontological nature of relation instances.""" <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#sameAs> "To enable more inferences, you could add a subclass axiom such that RRelTempProperPart is a subclass of RRelTempPart.\n\nWe do not include it here to avoid committment on the ontological nature of relation instances." .
We introduce classes of n-ary reified relationships and an object property for each argument of the n-ary relation.
We seek feedback especially regarding whether users understand or not what are the classes and the relations and how to use them.
